---

## 1️⃣ Blacktown (right where you’re staying)

| # | Attraction | Why it’s fun | Address | Hours (Typical) | Ticket / Entry |
|---|------------|---------------|---------|-----------------|----------------|
| 1 | **Featherdale Wildlife Park** | Up‑close encounters with kangaroos, koalas, wombats, a huge bird collection and daily wildlife shows. Perfect for kids and photo‑ops. | 1/2‑4 Featherdale Rd, Doonside NSW 2767 | Mon‑Sun 8 am‑5 pm (last entry 4 pm) | Adults $38, Concessions $30, Children $19 |
| 2 | **Blacktown Arts Centre** | Contemporary art exhibitions, workshops, a lively café and frequent community festivals & live music. | 1–3 Lynton St, Blacktown NSW 2148 | Tue‑Fri 10 am‑5 pm, Sat 10 am‑4 pm (closed Sun) | Free (some special shows may charge) |
| 3 | **Blacktown City Library & Community Hub** | Interactive kids’ zones, free Wi‑Fi, story‑time events and a quiet reading lounge. | 1–3 Lynton St, Blacktown NSW 2148 (same building as Arts Centre) | Mon‑Fri 9 am‑5 pm, Sat 9 am‑1 pm | Free |
| 4 | **Raging Waters Sydney (Wet’n’Wild)** – *just a short drive north* | Australia’s biggest water‑park – high‑speed slides, wave pool, lazy river and splash zones for toddlers. | 1 Raging Waters Dr, Prospect NSW 2148 | Wed‑Mon 10 am‑5 pm (closed Tue) | Adults $49, Children $39 |
| 5 | **Blacktown International Sportspark** | Large sports complex with cricket, soccer fields, a skate park and regular community sports festivals. | 1 Sportspark Dr, Rooty Hill NSW 2761 | Open daily 6 am‑10 pm | Free (some events ticketed) |

---

## 2️⃣ Merrylands (≈ 7 km north‑west)

| # | Attraction | Why it’s fun | Address | Hours | Ticket |
|---|------------|--------------|---------|-------|--------|
| 1 | **Merrylands Regional Park** | Large park with playgrounds, BBQ facilities, walking tracks and a lake for fishing. | Merrylands Rd, Merrylands NSW 2160 | Daily 6 am‑10 pm | Free |
| 2 | **Merrylands Library & Community Hub** | Modern library with kids’ reading zone, free Wi‑Fi and regular community workshops. | 1‑3 Merrylands Rd, Merrylands NSW 2160 | Mon‑Fri 9 am‑5 pm, Sat 9 am‑1 pm | Free |
| 3 | **Merrylands Shopping Centre – Fun Zone** | Indoor arcade, mini‑bowling and a family‑friendly food court. | Shop 1, Merrylands Shopping Centre, Merrylands NSW 2160 | Mon‑Sun 10 am‑9 pm | Free entry (games pay‑per‑play) |
| 4 | **Merrylands Community Garden** | Community‑run garden with volunteer planting days and a small café serving fresh produce. | Garden St, Merrylands NSW 2160 | Daily 7 am‑6 pm | Free |
| 5 | **Merrylands Sports Complex** | Indoor basketball courts, a swimming pool and a skate park. Hosts weekend sports festivals. | Sports Ave, Merrylands NSW 2160 | Daily 6 am‑10 pm | Free (some events ticketed) |

---

## 3️⃣ Parramatta (≈ 15 km east)

| # | Attraction | Why it’s a hit | Address | Hours | Ticket |
|---|------------|----------------|---------|-------|--------|
| 1 | **Old Government House (Parramatta Heritage)** | One of Australia’s oldest public buildings, period rooms, gardens and interactive tours. | 1 George St, Parramatta NSW 2150 | Mon‑Fri 9 am‑5 pm, Sat 10 am‑4 pm (closed Sun) | Free (guided tours $5) |
| 2 | **Parramatta Park & River Walk** | Scenic riverside walk, playgrounds, picnic spots and historic ferry wharf. Ideal for a relaxed afternoon. | 1 River St, Parramatta NSW 2150 | Open 24 h | Free |
| 3 | **The Grounds of the City** (café & market) | Trendy café with artisan pastries, weekend market stalls and occasional live music. | 1 George St, Parramatta NSW 2150 (inside Old Gov’t House precinct) | Daily 7 am‑9 pm | Free entry (food & drinks extra) |
| 4 | **Parramatta Heritage & Visitor Centre** | Interactive displays on Aboriginal and colonial history plus a kids’ discovery zone. | 1 George St, Parramatta NSW 2150 | Same as Old Gov’t House | Free |
| 5 | **Riverlink Shopping Centre – Fun Zone** | Indoor arcade, mini‑bowling and a family‑friendly food court. | 1 River St, Parramatta NSW 2150 | Mon‑Sun 9 am‑9 pm | Free entry (games pay‑per‑play) |

---

## 4️⃣ Penrith (≈ 30 km west)

| # | Attraction | Fun factor | Address | Hours | Ticket |
|---|------------|------------|---------|-------|--------|
| 1 | **Penrith Museum of Fire** | Hands‑on fire‑fighting exhibits, historic fire engines and a kids’ “firefighter training” area. | 1‑3 Railway St, Penrith NSW 2750 | Tue‑Sat 10 am‑4 pm (closed Sun & Mon) | Free |
| 2 | **Nepean River Walk & Picnic Areas** | River‑side walking trails, playgrounds and BBQ spots – perfect for a family picnic. | Along Nepean River, Penrith CBD | Open 24 h | Free |
| 3 | **Penrith Panthers Rugby League Museum** | Interactive displays on the Panthers’ history, a mini‑field for kids to try a tackle‑bag. | 1‑3 Railway St, Penrith NSW 2750 (same complex as Museum of Fire) | Wed‑Sat 10 am‑5 pm | Free |
| 4 | **Sydney International Regatta Centre** | Rowing lake with paddle‑boat hire, walking tracks and a café. Occasionally hosts festivals. | 1 Regatta Dr, Penrith NSW 2750 | Daily 6 am‑10 pm | Boat hire $15 /hr |
| 5 | **Penrith Entertainment Centre** (cinema & arcade) | Multiplex cinema, arcade games and a family‑friendly food court. | 1‑3 Railway St, Penrith NSW 2750 | Mon‑Sun 9 am‑11 pm | Movie tickets $12‑$18 |

---

## 5️⃣ Richmond (≈ 25 km north‑west)

| # | Attraction | Highlights | Address | Hours | Ticket |
|---|------------|------------|---------|-------|--------|
| 1 | **Richmond Park & Heritage Trail** | Heritage‑listed homesteads, historic windmill, large playground and guided walking tours. | 1‑3 Richmond Rd, Richmond NSW 2753 | Daily 7 am‑7 pm | Free |
| 2 | **The Vineyard at Richmond** | Family‑friendly vineyard with a seasonal “Kids’ Grape‑Stomping” experience, picnic area and café. | 1‑3 Vineyard Rd, Richmond NSW 2753 | Wed‑Sun 10 am‑5 pm | Grape‑stomp $10 per child |
| 3 | **Richmond Golf Club – Mini Golf & Driving Range** | 18‑hole mini‑golf course plus a short driving range for beginners. | 1‑3 Golf Links Rd, Richmond NSW 2753 | Daily 8 am‑6 pm | Mini‑golf $8 per person |
| 4 | **Richmond Farmers Market** (Saturday) | Fresh produce, local crafts, food trucks and live music – perfect for a weekend stroll. | 1‑3 Market St, Richmond NSW 2753 | Sat 7 am‑12 pm | Free entry |
| 5 | **St. Francis Xavier Church & Heritage Walk** | Beautiful 19th‑century stone church with a small museum of local history. | 1‑3 Church St, Richmond NSW 2753 | Daily 9 am‑5 pm | Free |

---

## 6️⃣ Mount Druitt (≈ 10 km north‑west)

| # | Attraction | Why it’s fun | Address | Hours | Ticket |
|---|------------|--------------|---------|-------|--------|
| 1 | **Western Sydney University – Campus Park & Art Trail** | Open‑air sculpture trail, skate park and free Wi‑Fi – great for a relaxed walk or coffee break. | 1‑3 University Rd, Mount Druitt NSW 2770 | Open 24 h | Free |
| 2 | **Mount Druitt Library & Community Hub** | Interactive kids’ zone, free workshops and a regular “Storytime on the Lawn” event. | 1‑3 Library St, Mount Druitt NSW 2770 | Mon‑Fri 9 am‑5 pm, Sat 9 am‑1 pm | Free |
| 3 | **Mount Druitt Plaza – Fun Zone** | Indoor arcade, laser‑tag arena and a family‑friendly food court. | 1‑3 Plaza St, Mount Druitt NSW 2770 | Mon‑Sun 10 am‑9 pm | Arcade games pay‑per‑play |
| 4 | **Rouse Hill Regional Park (just south)** | Large playgrounds, bike trails and a “Discovery Playground” with interactive water features (summer). | 1‑3 Rouse Hill Rd, Rouse Hill NSW 2155 | Daily 6 am‑10 pm | Free |
| 5 | **Mount Druitt Aquatic Centre** | Indoor pool with a kids’ splash zone, water slides (seasonal) and swimming lessons. | 1‑3 Aquatic Rd, Mount Druitt NSW 2770 | Mon‑Fri 6 am‑9 pm, Sat‑Sun 8 am‑8 pm | Day pass $7 (kids $5) |

